# Lazarus IDE-first UI

## Project stack

- **LazyCodingAgent** is a **Lazarus + LCL** desktop application (Free Pascal compiler under the hood).
- Default workflow: open `lazycodingagent.lpi` in the **Lazarus IDE**, edit forms in the **Form Designer**, build with the IDE or `lazbuild`.
- **No custom component package:** every visible control is a **stock LCL** type streamed in the form **`.lfm`** (`TPageControl`, `TTabSheet`, `TMemo`, `TComboBox`, `TButton`, `TSpeedButton`, `TSynEdit`, etc.). Open forms via the **`.pas`** file (F12), not a standalone `.lfm` tab. **Runtime-only (not in `.lfm`):** `TTerminalLCLView` (ViewLCL) via [`uTerminalPanel.pas`](uTerminalPanel.pas); **`TThemedPageTabBar`** on streamed **`TPanel`** tab-strip hosts via [`uThemedPageTabBar.pas`](uThemedPageTabBar.pas); **`TMarkdownHtmlView`** (TurboPower IpHtml) on streamed **`TPanel`** hosts for chat history, Markdown preview, and Help—via [`uMarkdownHtmlView.pas`](uMarkdownHtmlView.pas)—so the IDE needs no ViewLCL or custom tab design package.
- Do **not** treat this repo as a console-only or “code-only UI” FPC project. The main window and dialogs must remain **editable in Lazarus** for layout.

## Lazarus IDE contract (hard requirements)

### Layout lives in `.lfm`

- **`TForm`** uses paired **`.pas` + `.lfm`**, `{$R *.lfm}`, designer **`published`** fields, and `inherited` in constructors where applicable.
- Use normal **`TForm.Create(Application)`** or **`Create(AOwner)`** for modal dialogs—not `CreateNew` + manual `BuildForm` for user-facing UI.
- **Geometry and hierarchy** belong in the **`.lfm`** (`Align`, `Anchors`, tab order, captions). The **`.pas`** file holds **published** components and **event handlers** wired from the `.lfm`, plus business logic in `private` / `implementation`.
- Do **not** build designer-owned layout with **`TXXX.Create(Self)`** + manual **`SetBounds`** / parent assignment for new UI. Use the palette on the form instead.

### Standard LCL component palette only

- Use stock LCL controls from the component palette only.
- **Buttons:** designer **`TButton`**; optional `StylePrimaryButton` / `StyleCancelButton` / `StyleDestructiveButton` from [`uTheme.pas`](uTheme.pas). On **Windows**, [`uThemeWin32Buttons.pas`](uThemeWin32Buttons.pas) custom-paints those fills via `SetWindowSubclass` + `PaintThemedButton` (stock `TButton` in `.lfm` only). Linux/macOS use native widget colors (`TButton.Color`).
- **Tabs:** keep **`TPageControl`** / **`TTabSheet`** in **`.lfm`** with **`ShowTabs = False`**; use a stock **`TPanel`** tab-strip host in chrome; create **`TThemedPageTabBar`** at runtime in `FormCreate` (themed headers, optional **✕**, optional **`[+]`**).
- Apply look-and-feel at runtime via [`uTheme.pas`](uTheme.pas)—not other custom tab or button frame subclasses.
- **Do not reintroduce** removed bespoke UI: `uCustomTabControl`, `uDockPanel`, `uAppLogo`, `fraThemedTabs`, `fraThemedButton`, `fraThemedPicker`, `uMarkdownView`, or a Lazarus design package under `components/`. **`uPanelDetach`** is allowed for floating panels; detach controls are stock **`TButton`** (`⧉`) on panel chrome in `.lfm`.

### Published events and designer wiring

- Declare **published** components and event methods on the form class. Wire `OnCreate`, `OnClick`, `OnChange`, and similar in **`.lfm`** when the designer supports it.
- Any handler named in a `.lfm` must appear in the class **`published`** section (before `private`).

### Non-visual helpers (not layout owners)

- [`uNavigationPanel.pas`](uNavigationPanel.pas) — `TNavContentControl` binds to streamed nav labels, lists, tree, and buttons on `mainunit`.
- [`uChatPanel.pas`](uChatPanel.pas) — `TChatPanel` binds to streamed chat labels, `pnlChatHistoryHost`, prompt memo, combos, and buttons; creates **`TMarkdownHtmlView`** on the history host at runtime.
- [`uTerminalPanel.pas`](uTerminalPanel.pas) — PTY controller; creates **`TTerminalLCLView`** on the streamed `pnlTerminalContent` host at runtime.
- [`uThemedPageTabBar.pas`](uThemedPageTabBar.pas) — themed tab strip; created on streamed `pnl*TabStripHost` panels in [`mainunit.pas`](mainunit.pas) / [`frmSettings.pas`](frmSettings.pas) at runtime (not streamed).
- [`uMainFileEditor.pas`](uMainFileEditor.pas) / [`uPlanView.pas`](uPlanView.pas) — logic for streamed `TSynEdit` and plan utility controls.

Do **not** add new `TPanel` subclasses that `Create` child controls in Pascal.

## Main form layout ([`mainunit.lfm`](mainunit.lfm))

- **Nav rail:** one `TSpeedButton` per navigation item, `Align = alTop`, shared `GroupIndex`, `OnClick` in `.lfm`.
- **Nav body:** title/subtitle labels, `TListBox` / `TTreeView`, log list boxes, action buttons — visibility and captions only in code.
- **Center `TPageControl`:** Chat (history + composer + mode/model combos), Editor (`TSynEdit`), Markdown preview (`TPanel` host). One open file at a time; no per-file tab strip. Session name on the chat sheet; session list in **Sessions** nav.
- **Utility `TPageControl`:** Scratchpad, Execution Detail, Plan — fixed sheets.
- **Terminal:** chrome and status label on the bottom host in `.lfm`; `TTerminalLCLView` added at runtime. Panel **hide** (✕) only; no floating detach.

Regenerate the shell from [`scripts/gen-main-lfm.py`](scripts/gen-main-lfm.py) when adding rail items or large structural changes; preserve the `MainMenu1` tail.

## Theming (dark and light)

- Do **not** hardcode theme colors or fonts in `.lfm`. Runtime applies [`uTheme.pas`](uTheme.pas): `ApplyAllThemes`, `ApplyThemedControlTree`, `ApplyThemedForm`, `ThemePalette`, `StyleComboBox`, `ConfigureThemedListBox`, `ApplyPlatformChrome`; custom hooks via [`uThemeHooks.pas`](uThemeHooks.pas).
- Chat history, Markdown file preview, and Help topics use **`TMarkdownHtmlView`** on streamed **`TPanel`** hosts (rendered Markdown subset).

## When adding UI

1. Add or extend layout in the **Form Designer** (`.lfm`), usually [`mainunit.lfm`](mainunit.lfm) or a `frm*.lfm` dialog.
2. Wire events in `.lfm`; implement handlers in `.pas`.
3. After changes, verify **dark and light** via **View → Toggle Light / Dark Theme** and `lazbuild lazycodingagent.lpi`.
